    detailedDescriptionOfTheRole: "The Mobile Application Developer will be responsible for developing, integrating, testing, debugging, deploying, and maintaining cross-platform mobile applications throughout the Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC).\n\nThe developer will work with Flutter and Dart to build cross-platform mobile applications for supported Android and iOS environments. The role will include developing reusable widgets and components, implementing application screens, managing navigation, handling application state, integrating device functionality, and ensuring responsive behaviour across different screen sizes and device configurations.\n\nThe developer will also work with React Native using JavaScript and TypeScript to develop cross-platform mobile applications where applicable. The role will include developing reusable components, implementing mobile application workflows, managing navigation and state, integrating APIs, handling asynchronous operations, and maintaining application functionality across supported platforms.\n\nThe role will involve integrating mobile applications with RESTful APIs and backend services, including handling API requests and responses, JSON data, authentication, authorization, error handling, data validation, and secure communication between mobile applications and backend systems.\n\nThe Mobile Application Developer will be responsible for implementing mobile application interfaces based on approved UI/UX designs and ensuring consistency, usability, responsiveness, accessibility, and smooth user interaction across supported devices.\n\nThe developer will also work with local and remote data storage, application state management, caching, session handling, and data synchronization where required by the application.\n\nThe role will include application testing, debugging, performance optimisation, crash analysis, error handling, and issue resolution. The developer will collaborate with QA engineers to identify defects, reproduce issues, implement fixes, and validate application functionality before release.\n\nThe developer may also be involved in mobile application build generation, release preparation, application signing, deployment, version management, and publishing processes for Android and iOS platforms according to project requirements.\n\nThe Mobile Application Developer will use Git and GitHub for source-code management, version control, collaboration, branching, code review support, and maintenance of application code.\n\nThe role requires writing clean, reusable, maintainable, efficient, and well-structured code while following established development standards, security practices, documentation requirements, and project guidelines."
